body:

### Hi there :)

I’m Olena, a Software Engineer with 3 years of Python development experience. I started my engineering career with a cloud-native IoT project on AWS.

Currently I build backend microservices and data pipelines for a B2B product, and also dive into AI-driven automation (agent architecture and workflow orchestration) — now an essential part of the backend landscape.

Learning has always been an integral part of my life. I’ve spent a significant part of my career in data analysis and research, and had my first taste of scientific thinking during my university years. That background shaped my habit of constantly seeking insights and understanding not just *how* things work, but *why* they matter.

Beyond daily projects, I grow by contributing to open source, attending conferences and meetups, and I’m proud to be part of the Python community.

What I love most about this work is that there’s always something new to learn. I believe that *learning in public* leads to deeper understanding.

Here I write about:

- **Git workflows** and best practices for effective collaboration
- **Python core**: language internals, idiomatic patterns, and standard library gems
- **Testing strategies**: what to test, how to structure tests, and what actually works in production
- **Automating and deploying**: CI/CD, Docker, GitHub Actions, and infrastructure as code

*You can find my open source work and projects on [GitHub](https://github.com/OlenaYefymenko).*

Outside of work, I enjoy staying active: hiking, cycling, rollerblading, and skiing in winter.

Dance has always been part of my life — I studied choreography for years and still can’t resist a good song!
